<title>UK: EC may set conditions for Anglo/Lonrho deal - paper.</title>
<headline>EC may set conditions for Anglo/Lonrho deal - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is considering blocking Anglo-American Corp's acquisition of a 28 percent stake in rival Lonrho Plc unless the South African mining group agrees to make major concessions, said the Financial Times said on Friday.</p>
<p>Competition officials at the EC are understood to be concerned about the possible implications of the deal. and are preparing a list of objections to the purchase. The FT quoted one person close to the talks saying &quot;The statement of objections is very, very nasty.&quot;</p>
<p>The EC must rule by May 5. But the report said chances of clearance were slim.</p>
<p>Karel van Miert, competition commissioner at the EC, is understood to be against any move by Anglo-American to take control of Lonrho, said the FT.</p>
<p>He fears its stake in Lonrho would give the South African firm a dominant position in platinum and rodium markets.</p>
</text>
